# Versification "Bible Strong ThéoTeX Septuagint": an overlay on Paratext lxx.vrs, for the
# ThéoTeX Septuagint (LXX) and its French translation (LXX_FR), which number alike.
#
# Only the 66 books are described (decided 2026-11-27): the additions and the books outside
# them have no equivalent. A ThéoTeX verse that holds an addition in a lettered subdivision
# ("(a)", folded into the verse) keeps the equivalent of its verse.
#
# Mapping lines go from ThéoTeX to org. They were checked against the French translation
# (docs/research/versification.md, section 2.6).
#
1KI 5:31
2CH 27:8
EZR 11:0 12:0 13:0 14:0 15:0 16:0 17:0 18:0 19:0 20:0 21:0 22:0 23:0
NEH 1:11 2:20 3:37 4:17 5:19 6:19 7:73 8:18 9:37 10:40 11:32 12:47 13:31
EST 1:22 2:23 3:15 4:17 5:14 6:14 7:10 8:17 9:32 10:3
JOB 42:19
PRO 4:28
JER 34:21
DAN 1:21 2:49 3:97 4:37 5:30 6:29 7:28 8:27 9:27 10:21 11:45 12:13 13:64 14:41
#
# Numbers 26:1 ("Après la plaie, il advint que le Seigneur parla à Moïse…") opens with org 25:19,
# as in the English Bibles.
NUM 26:1 = NUM 25:19
NUM 26:1 = NUM 26:1
#
# ThéoTeX splits 2 Esdras into Ezra 1-10 and Nehemiah 1-13, numbered as org. LXX Nehemiah
# 7:68-69 ("{Sept cent trente-six chevaux…}", "{Quatre cent trente-cinq chameaux,} deux mille
# sept cents ânes.") is org 7:68.
#! &NEH 7:68-69 = NEH 7:68
NEH 7:70-73 = NEH 7:69-72
#
# Esther 1-10 is numbered as org; the Greek additions are lettered subdivisions of its verses.
#
# Daniel: the Prayer of Azariah and the Song of the Three (3:24-90), Susanna (13) and Bel and
# the Dragon (14) have no equivalent. LXX 3:91-97 is org 3:24-30, and LXX 4:1-3 ("Le roi
# Nabuchodonosor dit à tous les peuples…") is org 3:31-33, as in the English Bibles.
DAN 3:24-90 =
DAN 3:91-97 = DAN 3:24-30
DAN 4:1-3 = DAN 3:31-33
DAN 4:4-37 = DAN 4:1-34
DAN 13:1-64 =
DAN 14:1-41 =
#
# Job 42:18-19 (the Syriac note on Job's genealogy) and Proverbs 4:28 (4:27b, "Lui-même prendra
# soin de redresser les sentiers…") are additions.
JOB 42:18-19 =
PRO 4:28 =
#
# Jeremiah follows the Greek order, as lxx.vrs. Where lxx.vrs says a verse does not exist,
# ThéoTeX prints one row for the range: 32:1 "(1-13) Ainsi prophétisa Jérémie sur toutes les
# nations." is org 25:13, 32:14 "(14-15)" is org 25:15, and 46:4 "(4-14)" is org 39:14.
JER 32:1 = JER 25:13
JER 32:2-12 =
JER 32:14 = JER 25:15
JER 46:4 = JER 39:14
JER 46:5-13 =
